FIX FE SOUND-VOLUME SCREEN (822): reconstruct View_Sound_Volume @0x44e120 + int-type handler

Config rec-1 "Sound Volume" (Config nested table @0x46918c rec-1 ACTION 0x44e120) drilled into
an interactive volume slider that Ghidra never decompiled -> raw VA in the dispatch -> trapped
on wasm. Its descriptor @0x468b30 (stride 0x14, handler-fn @+4) points cat-0 at FUN_0044e308,
which DID decompile but was typed void and unregistered -> even once the main fn was callable,
`call [0x468b34]` (the label handler) would call_indirect a void fn under a code=int() site.

Reconstructed 1:1 from objdump of dd2h.exe:
- View_Sound_Volume @0x44e120: single "Sound Effects" slider (the "Music" sibling thunk
  0x44e2e6 is dead code -- unreferenced in the image). Volume working-copy @0x93fd20, range
  [0,0xffa] step 0x199, committed to @0x467410 + applied via FUN_00415ba0 on exit. Pad bits
  match the other viewers (0x80/0x20 vol down/up via pad word 0x754448; 0x10/0x40 category nav;
  0x4000 accept; 0x1000 back). int(void) to match the nested code=int() dispatch.
- FUN_0044e308 widened void->int (+return 0), registered so dd2_relocate rewrites the
  descriptor slot 0x468b34 to a real table index.

Same unreconstructed/int-typing class as View Statistics (821) + patches 816/817/818.
Disproves the "toolchain call_indirect bug" for this screen too: the trap was unregistered
raw-VA handlers, not a binaryen anomaly.

